WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.260 --> 00:00:02.790
Think back to your childhood for a moment.

00:00:02.790 --> 00:00:07.260
When you used to play hide and seek, where
was your go-to hiding spot, the one place

00:00:07.260 --> 00:00:11.150
you knew for sure that no one would ever be
able to find you?

00:00:11.150 --> 00:00:16.020
Outdoors it might have been inside a garden
shed or garage, or maybe you had a treehouse

00:00:16.020 --> 00:00:19.930
where you could lay low as the seekers searched
hopelessly for you.

00:00:19.930 --> 00:00:25.560
Indoors, on the other hand, normally no hiding
place can beat a wardrobe, closet, or cabinet

00:00:25.560 --> 00:00:28.820
when it comes to keeping yourself totally
undetected.

00:00:28.820 --> 00:00:32.720
But what if there was a cabinet you could
find yourself getting lost in?

00:00:32.720 --> 00:00:36.399
Something that looks small from the outside
but that contains an unknowable amount of

00:00:36.399 --> 00:00:38.370
interior space within?

00:00:38.370 --> 00:00:44.260
We call it SCP-432, although some of the researchers
have given it the rather adequate nickname

00:00:44.260 --> 00:00:46.159
of the Cabinet Maze.

00:00:46.159 --> 00:00:51.850
And it is why you are here, why we at the
SCP Foundation have gathered you; because

00:00:51.850 --> 00:00:56.120
you’ll be our next expedition inside SCP-432.

00:00:56.120 --> 00:01:00.590
Now, before you start to argue, we’re not
going to send you in there empty-handed.

00:01:00.590 --> 00:01:04.860
You’ll be provided with the standard equipment
for a mission like this.

00:01:04.860 --> 00:01:09.220
Make sure you’ve got your handheld flashlight
with you and enough additional batteries.

00:01:09.220 --> 00:01:13.160
Your headsets have a microphone that will
relay audio back to us back at control, and

00:01:13.160 --> 00:01:16.530
we’ll be watching everything through the
camera units you will each have mounted to

00:01:16.530 --> 00:01:17.780
your shoulder.

00:01:17.780 --> 00:01:22.390
You should also take two bottles of water
each, and the same in energy bars.

00:01:22.390 --> 00:01:26.610
We said only two, don’t try to sneak any
extra, we’ll know!

00:01:26.610 --> 00:01:29.410
Finally, you all need eight sticks of these
chalk markers.

00:01:29.410 --> 00:01:35.390
They’re luminous; you’re going to be leaving
indicators once inside SCP-432, and that will

00:01:35.390 --> 00:01:37.120
help you navigate your way around.

00:01:37.120 --> 00:01:39.280
Well, they should help.

00:01:39.280 --> 00:01:40.280
Hopefully…

00:01:40.280 --> 00:01:45.720
As some of you may have heard, this will not
be our first expedition into SCP-432, and

00:01:45.720 --> 00:01:48.000
likely won’t be our last either.

00:01:48.000 --> 00:01:52.409
Although it’s highly irregular, given the
‘complications’ encountered on our previous

00:01:52.409 --> 00:01:56.890
missions, we’ll be providing you with some
select details relating to a few of these

00:01:56.890 --> 00:01:59.590
aforementioned prior investigations.

00:01:59.590 --> 00:02:03.090
If you were all paying attention when you
were first briefed about this, then you’ll

00:02:03.090 --> 00:02:09.379
already be aware that SCP-432 is a steel storage
cabinet first discovered in an abandoned industrial

00:02:09.379 --> 00:02:11.560
complex in the UK.

00:02:11.560 --> 00:02:15.610
Of course, if that’s all it was then we
wouldn’t be sending you into it.

00:02:15.610 --> 00:02:20.959
The first expedition into SCP-432 didn’t
involve a group anywhere near this size, that

00:02:20.959 --> 00:02:23.969
time we just sent one D Class into the cabinet.

00:02:23.969 --> 00:02:29.310
Once he had stepped inside, his camera feed
showed us our first recorded look at the interior.

00:02:29.310 --> 00:02:33.290
From what we could see, the D Class was standing
in a corridor that had been constructed out

00:02:33.290 --> 00:02:37.249
of the same corroded, rusty metal as the outer
cabinet.

00:02:37.249 --> 00:02:41.930
Following our instructions given via his headset,
this D Class subject – actually, let’s

00:02:41.930 --> 00:02:47.579
call him Max – continued down this corridor,
turning around a corner a few meters from

00:02:47.579 --> 00:02:49.040
where he’d entered.

00:02:49.040 --> 00:02:54.150
Max saw a further, longer tunnel ahead, although
the poor level of lighting made it impossible

00:02:54.150 --> 00:02:56.400
to judge just how far it stretched.

00:02:56.400 --> 00:03:01.540
There was an ordinary electric lightbulb illuminating
part of this corridor, but not enough to make

00:03:01.540 --> 00:03:03.680
more that a few short meters visible.

00:03:03.680 --> 00:03:08.319
By the light of his torch, Max followed this
tunnel over forty meters until it split off

00:03:08.319 --> 00:03:13.279
in varying directions; almost like a crossroads
of corroded metal.

00:03:13.279 --> 00:03:17.459
After conferring with Control, Max made a
mark on the wall nearby, pointing back the

00:03:17.459 --> 00:03:19.519
way he came, towards the exit.

00:03:19.519 --> 00:03:23.480
That’s an important tip for all of you to
remember; use the equipment we’ve issued

00:03:23.480 --> 00:03:26.400
you with in order to find your way back to
safety…

00:03:26.400 --> 00:03:30.349
well, try to at least, even if it doesn’t
work.

00:03:30.349 --> 00:03:34.290
Making his way down the left tunnel, it was
at this point that Max’s video feed began

00:03:34.290 --> 00:03:36.099
to degrade in quality.

00:03:36.099 --> 00:03:40.319
From the safety of the Control room, Foundation
technicians noted staticky lines of interference

00:03:40.319 --> 00:03:42.510
shooting across their monitors.

00:03:42.510 --> 00:03:46.950
After traversing another eleven meters, Max
arrived at a T-junction in the tunnels and

00:03:46.950 --> 00:03:50.919
again opted to follow the left path and marked
the way back with his chalk.

00:03:50.919 --> 00:03:53.999
It was after that turn that Max heard…

00:03:53.999 --> 00:03:55.019
something.

00:03:55.019 --> 00:04:00.150
The sound didn’t make its way back to Control
due to all the distortion and interference.

00:04:00.150 --> 00:04:04.249
When they asked him what he had heard, Max
waited a moment, listening out for the sound

00:04:04.249 --> 00:04:05.249
until…

00:04:05.249 --> 00:04:06.290
there it was again.

00:04:06.290 --> 00:04:10.769
As quietly as he could while still remaining
audible, he described the noise.

00:04:10.769 --> 00:04:16.570
Somewhere off in the distance, further down
the rust-coated corridor, someone or something

00:04:16.570 --> 00:04:18.420
was banging against the metal walls.

00:04:18.420 --> 00:04:24.350
There were even traces of a voice, shouting
fearfully into the dark labyrinth.

00:04:24.350 --> 00:04:28.160
Turning up the audio gain on Max’s camera,
the Foundation personnel at Control could

00:04:28.160 --> 00:04:29.670
hear it too.

00:04:29.670 --> 00:04:33.540
Noticeably shaken, the D Class continued down
the corridor in the direction of the banging

00:04:33.540 --> 00:04:38.970
and shouting, only for him to freeze as he
heard a new sound: someone screaming.

00:04:38.970 --> 00:04:41.500
The other noises had stopped immediately after.

00:04:41.500 --> 00:04:45.540
Max was getting more and more agitated, demanding
to be allowed to leave.

00:04:45.540 --> 00:04:48.370
But Control urged him to explore further.

00:04:48.370 --> 00:04:52.620
Arriving at another T-junction, he instead
went right this time, once more using his

00:04:52.620 --> 00:04:54.780
chalk to leave a marker.

00:04:54.780 --> 00:04:58.830
This is your gentle reminder that you all
need to make this a habit when you go into

00:04:58.830 --> 00:04:59.830
SCP-432.

00:04:59.830 --> 00:05:05.040
The right side tunnel of this junction led
to a dead-end and doubling back to try the

00:05:05.040 --> 00:05:08.100
left hand one only ended up yielding the same
result.

00:05:08.100 --> 00:05:13.170
By this point, it had only been thirty-seven
minutes since Max had first entered SCP-432,

00:05:13.170 --> 00:05:19.280
and the Foundation doctor assigned to the
cabinet decided that was enough for expedition

00:05:19.280 --> 00:05:20.280
one.

00:05:20.280 --> 00:05:24.690
Max was recalled, ordered to return to the
entrance, and began doubling back the way

00:05:24.690 --> 00:05:25.690
he’d come.

00:05:25.690 --> 00:05:30.190
He stopped at the crossroads, remarking that
he’d heard another noise, and Control had

00:05:30.190 --> 00:05:32.330
picked up the same thing.

00:05:32.330 --> 00:05:37.030
This time it was the sound of the wind, a
gentle breeze was blowing through the tunnel

00:05:37.030 --> 00:05:39.460
from somewhere deeper within the maze.

00:05:39.460 --> 00:05:43.440
Max’s camera captured a few dead leaves
drifting through one of the tunnels he hadn’t

00:05:43.440 --> 00:05:44.440
yet explored.

00:05:44.440 --> 00:05:48.860
He was commanded to collect the leaves for
analysis, much to his disapproval; by this

00:05:48.860 --> 00:05:50.760
point, he clearly wanted out.

00:05:50.760 --> 00:05:54.820
As Max followed the order and drew nearer
to the uncharted corridor, the deafening sound

00:05:54.820 --> 00:05:58.920
of a roar echoed through the tunnel, sounding
like that of a bear or a lion.

00:05:58.920 --> 00:06:03.840
In a panic, Max dashed back the way he’d
come, directed by the chalk markings he’d

00:06:03.840 --> 00:06:05.360
left on the walls.

00:06:05.360 --> 00:06:09.060
Foundation Control demanded that he go back
and investigate the source of the roaring,

00:06:09.060 --> 00:06:13.120
but he was beyond the point of listening now,
desperate to get away from the dark tangled

00:06:13.120 --> 00:06:16.370
mass of dimly lit metal tunnels.

00:06:16.370 --> 00:06:21.780
Screaming as he ran, Max sprinted through
the SCP-432 cabinet, collapsing from the sheer,

00:06:21.780 --> 00:06:23.580
overwhelming rush of terror.

00:06:23.580 --> 00:06:28.420
Now much like the first, expedition number
two only utilized a single member of D Class

00:06:28.420 --> 00:06:30.200
to explore more of SCP-432.

00:06:30.200 --> 00:06:35.450
Obviously, there’s only so much ground one
person can cover, which is why we’ve recruited

00:06:35.450 --> 00:06:37.650
so many of you for the next excursion.

00:06:37.650 --> 00:06:41.960
Don’t worry, we’ve already run the numbers
and calculated just how many of you will make

00:06:41.960 --> 00:06:43.750
it back in one piece.

00:06:43.750 --> 00:06:48.110
From the moment the subject of this second
outing – who we’ll call Kari – was sent

00:06:48.110 --> 00:06:54.140
into SCP-432, her camera feed showed something
particularly striking.

00:06:54.140 --> 00:06:58.800
The interior of the Cabinet Maze seemed to
differ from how it began during expedition

00:06:58.800 --> 00:06:59.800
one.

00:06:59.800 --> 00:07:03.720
It was as if the extradimensional space within
the metal storage cupboard had somehow changed

00:07:03.720 --> 00:07:07.670
itself, reconfiguring into a different layout.

00:07:07.670 --> 00:07:12.490
Instructed by Control, Kari walked slowly
down a long, straight corridor, which continued

00:07:12.490 --> 00:07:17.920
forward for about a hundred meters before
splitting into a two-way T-junction.

00:07:17.920 --> 00:07:23.190
Taking the right-hand route and leaving behind
a marker, she proceeded a further fifty meters.

00:07:23.190 --> 00:07:28.260
This time around, the tunnels within SCP-432
were illuminated more frequently by lightbulbs,

00:07:28.260 --> 00:07:34.540
but not quite enough; Kari still needed her
torch to see a little further into the darkness.

00:07:34.540 --> 00:07:39.090
She reached a crossroads, although it lacked
any chalk markings, meaning it was not the

00:07:39.090 --> 00:07:41.990
same as the one first encountered by Max.

00:07:41.990 --> 00:07:46.230
Control commanded Kari to take the left side
tunnel after leaving her own marker, and she

00:07:46.230 --> 00:07:50.080
then followed this new route until hitting
a second crossroads.

00:07:50.080 --> 00:07:55.330
However, acting without orders from the Foundation,
Kari took the right side passageway.

00:07:55.330 --> 00:07:58.840
Despite admonishment from Control, she was
allowed to continue.

00:07:58.840 --> 00:08:03.050
However, we would advise following any and
all instructions put to you for the duration

00:08:03.050 --> 00:08:07.250
of time that you are inside SCP-432 later
on.

00:08:07.250 --> 00:08:11.920
Ahead of her, Kari’s torchlight showed there
to be a third crossroads, but something caused

00:08:11.920 --> 00:08:14.420
her to stop before she got closer.

00:08:14.420 --> 00:08:18.650
She reported the noise of a rhythmic banging
that reverberated through the rusted metal

00:08:18.650 --> 00:08:20.560
walls of the labyrinth.

00:08:20.560 --> 00:08:25.070
Staying perfectly still, trying to keep her
breathing low and quiet, Kari nervously asked

00:08:25.070 --> 00:08:31.210
about what SCP-432 really was, and where that
ominous sound was coming from.

00:08:31.210 --> 00:08:35.729
Naturally, Foundation Control did not provide
any answers.

00:08:35.729 --> 00:08:40.070
As Kari delved further into the labyrinth,
her camera feed showed a number of the lightbulbs

00:08:40.070 --> 00:08:44.560
in this corridor had been shattered, leaving
shards of glass on the metal floor.

00:08:44.560 --> 00:08:49.120
Additionally, she noted that there was an
unpleasant, stomach-churning odor in the air,

00:08:49.120 --> 00:08:51.370
that smelled like something dead.

00:08:51.370 --> 00:08:55.300
Kari noticed an object a few meters later,
although her camera feed was beginning to

00:08:55.300 --> 00:08:58.950
cut in and out as she knelt down to examine
what it was.

00:08:58.950 --> 00:09:04.279
She reported it was a sports sneaker, but
as her camera refocused on the abandoned footwear,

00:09:04.279 --> 00:09:07.910
the feed suddenly shifted angles, tilting
down towards the floor…

00:09:07.910 --> 00:09:10.270
that was covered in blood.

00:09:10.270 --> 00:09:12.490
Kari hadn’t realized what it was at first.

00:09:12.490 --> 00:09:17.940
There was a layer of a dried brown substance
on the corridor floor, flaking off in places.

00:09:17.940 --> 00:09:22.410
Looking up under the light of her torch, Kari
noticed even more had been over the walls,

00:09:22.410 --> 00:09:27.260
although it must have been some time ago given
how the blood had long started to dry out

00:09:27.260 --> 00:09:28.260
and crackle.

00:09:28.260 --> 00:09:33.550
But that did little to make her feel comfortable
at the sight of a long smear trailing away

00:09:33.550 --> 00:09:35.590
up the corridor.

00:09:35.590 --> 00:09:39.810
Despite her continued complaints about the
sickening, decaying smell, Control instructed

00:09:39.810 --> 00:09:43.510
Kari to collect the shoe and samples of the
dried blood for testing.

00:09:43.510 --> 00:09:49.120
She asked to be let out of SCP-432, but the
Foundation personnel denied her request, telling

00:09:49.120 --> 00:09:54.590
her to continue further down the corridor,
which she did at a much slower, more reluctant

00:09:54.590 --> 00:09:55.590
pace.

00:09:55.590 --> 00:09:59.810
It was only when her video and audio feeds
started to suffer heavy interference that

00:09:59.810 --> 00:10:02.130
Control told her to return.

00:10:02.130 --> 00:10:06.080
By now, Kari was panicking, saying she could
hear footsteps behind one of the walls and

00:10:06.080 --> 00:10:08.900
made her way back out at a far quicker speed.

00:10:08.900 --> 00:10:13.640
For security reasons, details pertaining to
the Foundation’s third SCP-432 expedition

00:10:13.640 --> 00:10:15.330
cannot be shared with you all.

00:10:15.330 --> 00:10:19.480
Don’t worry, we can still provide you with
information about the fourth and fifth attempts

00:10:19.480 --> 00:10:22.870
before you end up heading into the Cabinet
Maze yourselves.

00:10:22.870 --> 00:10:28.089
In a departure from the initial two, the fourth
of our expeditions featured a team of three

00:10:28.089 --> 00:10:33.560
personnel; two from D Class – who will be
referred to as Leo and Jade – and one SCP

00:10:33.560 --> 00:10:35.990
Foundation Technical Assistant, ‘Kay’.

00:10:35.990 --> 00:10:40.590
We aren’t currently planning on sending
any more of our own ranks into SCP-432, so

00:10:40.590 --> 00:10:43.670
when you venture in there you’ll only have
each other for company...

00:10:43.670 --> 00:10:46.990
plus whatever else is inside the labyrinth.

00:10:46.990 --> 00:10:50.770
Some of the standard exploration equipment
was divided up amongst the group, with only

00:10:50.770 --> 00:10:54.180
Leo given the luminous chalk markers, as well
as a prybar.

00:10:54.180 --> 00:10:59.150
Jade was the only member given a shoulder-mounted
video unit, and for their own safety, Kay

00:10:59.150 --> 00:11:00.910
was issued with a firearm.

00:11:00.910 --> 00:11:06.850
The primary objective of this exploration
of SCP-432 was to use an oxyacetylene cutting

00:11:06.850 --> 00:11:11.690
torch – operated by Kay – to cut through
the corroded metal walls of the corridors

00:11:11.690 --> 00:11:12.690
within.

00:11:12.690 --> 00:11:16.620
Venturing inside, the team made their way
along a series of turns that Foundation Control

00:11:16.620 --> 00:11:17.980
chose at random.

00:11:17.980 --> 00:11:22.720
They arrived at a crossroads, immediately
noticing something that hadn’t been present

00:11:22.720 --> 00:11:24.880
during the earlier expeditions.

00:11:24.880 --> 00:11:29.190
The northmost passageway of the crossroads
had two large steel pipes attached to the

00:11:29.190 --> 00:11:33.790
walls, almost like those found in factories
or other industrial settings.

00:11:33.790 --> 00:11:38.220
Upon receiving a message from Control to examine
the pipes, Kay remarked that the metalwork

00:11:38.220 --> 00:11:42.970
was cold to the touch, seemingly with liquid
passing through them as if these were some

00:11:42.970 --> 00:11:44.930
form of plumbing system.

00:11:44.930 --> 00:11:49.430
Kay requested to cut the pipes open using
their blowtorch, but Control denied and instructed

00:11:49.430 --> 00:11:51.120
the group to follow them instead.

00:11:51.120 --> 00:11:55.740
They did so for around three hundred meters,
only to find the pipes continued through a

00:11:55.740 --> 00:11:58.220
wall that blocked the team’s path.

00:11:58.220 --> 00:12:03.090
Under orders to do so, Kay ignited the oxyacetylene
torch and began attempting to cut through

00:12:03.090 --> 00:12:06.190
the metal surface that stood like a dead end
in their way.

00:12:06.190 --> 00:12:10.839
It was at that point that Jade reported hearing
something behind them, although a sweep of

00:12:10.839 --> 00:12:13.220
her camera showed the corridor was empty.

00:12:13.220 --> 00:12:17.320
Or, at the very least, it appeared to be empty.

00:12:17.320 --> 00:12:21.910
Having made a few cuts into the metal wall,
Kay then allowed Leo to use his prybar to

00:12:21.910 --> 00:12:26.710
try and lever a section of it open to allow
the group a way to climb through.

00:12:26.710 --> 00:12:31.040
The moment he did, a loud roar was heard coming
from behind the wall.

00:12:31.040 --> 00:12:35.810
The terrifying, animalistic sound caused Jade
to scream, backing away in fear.

00:12:35.810 --> 00:12:40.300
Only for something on the other side of the
metal to punch at the blowtorched wall, with

00:12:40.300 --> 00:12:43.790
enough force to bend its rusted surface outwards.

00:12:43.790 --> 00:12:48.520
The video feed from Jade’s camera unit began
to sporadically cut in and out, along with

00:12:48.520 --> 00:12:49.520
the audio.

00:12:49.520 --> 00:12:53.140
But what did come through were clear sounds
of a struggle.

00:12:53.140 --> 00:12:57.930
Violent roaring and gunfire from Kay’s sidearm,
along with screaming from all three members

00:12:57.930 --> 00:12:59.700
of the exploration team.

00:12:59.700 --> 00:13:05.310
There was something else inside the Cabinet
Maze, some indigenous lifeform that roamed

00:13:05.310 --> 00:13:11.630
the long, dark metal corridors, that was now
attacking the latest three to venture inside.

00:13:11.630 --> 00:13:15.470
Only Jade made it back to the entrance of
the labyrinth, by following the chalk markers

00:13:15.470 --> 00:13:17.850
the group had been leaving on the walls along
the way.

00:13:17.850 --> 00:13:21.930
It’s because of how effective this practice
is that we’ve been encouraging you to make

00:13:21.930 --> 00:13:24.910
sure you do the same once inside SCP-432.

00:13:24.910 --> 00:13:31.130
By the time this D Class returned, she was
in a clear state of complete and utter distress,

00:13:31.130 --> 00:13:33.560
as well as severely injured.

00:13:33.560 --> 00:13:36.500
She was covered in blood, not all of it her
own.

00:13:36.500 --> 00:13:41.560
Neither Jade’s fellow D Class Leo nor Foundation
Technical Assistant Kay made it back.

00:13:41.560 --> 00:13:47.131
The personnel waiting outside the rusty cabinet
had to shut SCP-432 after Jade emerged, in

00:13:47.131 --> 00:13:50.440
order to prevent whatever creature was inside
from escaping.

00:13:50.440 --> 00:13:54.430
When they re-opened the doors after enough
time had elapsed, the interior corridors of

00:13:54.430 --> 00:14:00.250
SCP-432 had reconfigured themselves again,
meaning the other two members of expedition

00:14:00.250 --> 00:14:02.220
four were lost.

00:14:02.220 --> 00:14:07.360
As for D Class member D-8321, she was terminated
shortly after being debriefed.

00:14:07.360 --> 00:14:11.910
What was perhaps most curious about this though,
was that Foundation personnel found a large

00:14:11.910 --> 00:14:17.160
tuft of brown animal hair had been caught
in her equipment harness, presumably during

00:14:17.160 --> 00:14:18.160
the attack.

00:14:18.160 --> 00:14:22.820
The hair smelt notably unpleasant, but analysis
showed that it belonged to a known family

00:14:22.820 --> 00:14:23.820
of animal.

00:14:23.820 --> 00:14:27.870
However, there were also a number of notable
irregularities within its DNA.

00:14:27.870 --> 00:14:31.580
Now, that brings us on to expedition number
five.

00:14:31.580 --> 00:14:36.320
In a return to form, only a single member
of D Class – we’ll call him Mike – was

00:14:36.320 --> 00:14:41.850
sent into SCP-432 this time; though, naturally
during your exploration there will be a few

00:14:41.850 --> 00:14:45.010
more of you making your way through those
corridors.

00:14:45.010 --> 00:14:49.070
Possibly the most noticeable difference between
this excursion and all of those that had previously

00:14:49.070 --> 00:14:54.850
been conducted was that now no light was being
emitted within the corroded metal tunnels.

00:14:54.850 --> 00:14:59.700
All the lightbulbs that had once offered at
least a low level of visibility were now smashed,

00:14:59.700 --> 00:15:04.510
with Mike noticing there was a substantial
amount of broken glass littering the floor.

00:15:04.510 --> 00:15:08.860
Perhaps the creature in there got bored and
broke them all… or maybe it wanted the advantage

00:15:08.860 --> 00:15:11.149
of no one being able to see it.

00:15:11.149 --> 00:15:16.250
Guided by the instructions Control were issuing,
Mike followed a short corridor about ten meters

00:15:16.250 --> 00:15:20.810
along, before stopping at his first of the
T-junctions that seemed to regularly occur

00:15:20.810 --> 00:15:22.800
within the Cabinet Maze.

00:15:22.800 --> 00:15:27.510
Making a left as Control told him to, Mike
kept his torch on, pointing ahead of him to

00:15:27.510 --> 00:15:29.540
alleviate some of the dark.

00:15:29.540 --> 00:15:33.330
Following and marking each turning that Control
instructed that he take, much like all the

00:15:33.330 --> 00:15:38.649
previous expeditions, Mike reported hearing
strange noises coming from within the labyrinth.

00:15:38.649 --> 00:15:43.250
He described the sound of machinery emanating
from some distant part of the maze, as well

00:15:43.250 --> 00:15:45.860
as feeling cold.

00:15:45.860 --> 00:15:51.240
All the bulbs were still broken, and not one
that he came into contact with provided any

00:15:51.240 --> 00:15:52.240
light.

00:15:52.240 --> 00:15:56.820
Taking a break to drink some water and recharge
his energy with a ration bar, Mike had reached

00:15:56.820 --> 00:16:02.640
almost two and a half thousand meters into
SCP-432, making it deeper into the Cabinet

00:16:02.640 --> 00:16:04.650
Maze than anyone previously had…

00:16:04.650 --> 00:16:07.640
well, a member of personnel anyway.

00:16:07.640 --> 00:16:12.120
The reason we say that is because Mike soon
discovered signs that someone else might have

00:16:12.120 --> 00:16:14.320
been hiding within the labyrinth.

00:16:14.320 --> 00:16:19.660
He noticed a few old, crumpled tin cans and
a bent fork that had been used to eat their

00:16:19.660 --> 00:16:20.660
contents.

00:16:20.660 --> 00:16:26.930
Whoever else was that deep inside SCP-432
would likely not still be alive, especially

00:16:26.930 --> 00:16:31.279
with the creature lurking in the corridors;
although if they were, perhaps it was them

00:16:31.279 --> 00:16:33.670
who broke all the lights to keep themselves
hidden.

00:16:33.670 --> 00:16:38.690
Soon after, Mike overheard the sound of a
man sobbing coming from somewhere close by.

00:16:38.690 --> 00:16:42.430
Although Control struggled to hear the same,
they instructed Mike to follow the noise of

00:16:42.430 --> 00:16:45.000
crying and locate the person responsible.

00:16:45.000 --> 00:16:48.950
Chasing through the dark towards whoever it
was, Mike could hardly see a thing, even with

00:16:48.950 --> 00:16:50.770
his torch as a light source.

00:16:50.770 --> 00:16:51.770
“Hello?

00:16:51.770 --> 00:16:52.770
Can you hear me?

00:16:52.770 --> 00:16:56.240
I'm coming!” he called, trying to get the
attention of the weeping man.

00:16:56.240 --> 00:17:01.000
Instantly, a Foundation Control technician
in his earpiece told Mike not to raise his

00:17:01.000 --> 00:17:05.890
voice, reproaching the D Class and warning
that he could draw attention to himself.

00:17:05.890 --> 00:17:11.040
When Mike retorted by asking what else was
down in the corridors of SCP-432, no further

00:17:11.040 --> 00:17:12.329
answer was provided.

00:17:12.329 --> 00:17:17.809
He paused at the next junction where the tunnels
intersected, hearing a long, drawn-out moaning

00:17:17.809 --> 00:17:19.819
sound, possibly a scream.

00:17:19.819 --> 00:17:22.199
A human scream.

00:17:22.199 --> 00:17:24.280
The crying stopped immediately after.

00:17:24.280 --> 00:17:27.791
Mike asked Control if they had picked up the
sound, stating that it seemed to have come

00:17:27.791 --> 00:17:29.590
from somewhere nearby.

00:17:29.590 --> 00:17:33.590
Once again, Control urged him to continue
further into the labyrinth, although now Mike

00:17:33.590 --> 00:17:38.340
was trying to move as slowly, and stealthily,
as he possibly could.

00:17:38.340 --> 00:17:41.520
Turning a right corner about twenty meters
further down, Mike’s camera feed showed

00:17:41.520 --> 00:17:44.140
that he had reached yet another dead end.

00:17:44.140 --> 00:17:46.020
The maze blocked his way forward.

00:17:46.020 --> 00:17:51.260
Leaning his ear close to the metal, Mike listened
for any further signs of life, only to recoil

00:17:51.260 --> 00:17:54.370
at what he heard beyond the blocked corridor.

00:17:54.370 --> 00:18:00.970
Crunching, the noise of bones being broken,
and something… someone being eaten by the

00:18:00.970 --> 00:18:05.250
lifeform that resides within SCP-432.

00:18:05.250 --> 00:18:09.120
Control urged Mike to get out of there, and
he complied, although not without checking

00:18:09.120 --> 00:18:11.110
over his shoulder the whole walk back.

00:18:11.110 --> 00:18:14.890
At present, we still don’t have an accurate
description of the creature.

00:18:14.890 --> 00:18:20.530
Some theories state that it might be imprisoned
inside SCP-432, others suggest that it guards

00:18:20.530 --> 00:18:24.930
the labyrinth within and protects it from
trespassers and interlopers.

00:18:24.930 --> 00:18:28.450
As for how other human beings – or their
remains, at least – have been uncovered

00:18:28.450 --> 00:18:29.720
within the Cabinet Maze?

00:18:29.720 --> 00:18:33.740
Well, a number of homeless people had been
reported missing from the industrial complex

00:18:33.740 --> 00:18:36.740
where SCP-432 was first uncovered.

00:18:36.740 --> 00:18:42.710
Presumably, some of them used that area for
shelter and some ended up inside the cabinet.

00:18:42.710 --> 00:18:46.170
Of course, our current objective is to learn
more about the creature.

00:18:46.170 --> 00:18:47.580
This is where you all come in.

00:18:47.580 --> 00:18:51.850
So, now that we’ve covered the previous
expeditions into SCP-432.

00:18:51.850 --> 00:18:56.200
If there are no further questions, we’d
like you all to walk right this way.

00:18:56.200 --> 00:18:57.980
What are you waiting for?

00:18:57.980 --> 00:18:59.350
Step inside the cabinet.

00:18:59.350 --> 00:19:01.730
Of course, we’ll let you back out afterwards…

00:19:01.730 --> 00:19:08.320
Now go and check out “SCP-3333 TOWER”
and “SCP-5140 FROZEN BODIES ON EVEREST ARE

00:19:08.320 --> 00:19:12.570
ALIVE” for more anomalous areas you really
shouldn’t try to explore yourself.

00:19:12.570 --> 00:19:14.130
Don’t believe us?

00:19:14.130 --> 00:19:17.710
Maybe you’ll think twice about taking a
trip after you hear what’s waiting for you!

